    "content": {
      "value": "SFCC Project Onboarding\n=======================\n\nThis section provides a central onboarding hub for the Zimmermann SFCC Migration project. It is designed to help new team members, stakeholders, and delivery partners quickly understand the project context, ways of working, key contacts, governance routines, and required access or setup activities.\n\nOnboarding Objectives\n---------------------\n\n* Provide a clear starting point for anyone joining the SFCC Migration project.\n* Accelerate understanding of project scope, objectives, timelines, and delivery approach.\n* Ensure new joiners know where to find key project artefacts, tools, and communication channels.\n* Standardise access requests, environment setup, and role-specific onboarding activities.\n* Support consistent alignment with PMO governance, reporting, and escalation processes.\n\nWho This Section Is For\n-----------------------\n\n| Audience | Onboarding Focus |\n| --- | --- |\n| Zimmermann stakeholders | Project objectives, governance forums, decision-making process, milestone visibility, and escalation paths. |\n| Delivery team members | Scope, delivery plan, workstream responsibilities, tools, ceremonies, and ways of working. |\n| Technical team members | Architecture context, environments, access, integrations, release process, and development standards. |\n| PMO and project management team | Status reporting, RAID management, meeting cadence, governance artefacts, and action tracking. |\n\nRecommended Onboarding Path\n---------------------------\n\n1. Review the project overview, scope, and key objectives.\n2. Understand the SFCC Migration delivery timeline and major milestones.\n3. Confirm your project role, responsibilities, and primary workstream.\n4. Request access to required systems, tools, repositories, and communication channels.\n5. Review governance routines, reporting expectations, and meeting cadence.\n6. Complete role-specific onboarding activities and connect with your workstream lead.\n\nKey Onboarding Topics\n---------------------\n\n| Topic | Description | Owner |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Project Context | Background, business drivers, migration objectives, and success measures for the SFCC project. | Delivery Lead |\n| Scope and Workstreams | Overview of in-scope capabilities, delivery workstreams, dependencies, and ownership. | Project Manager |\n| Governance and Cadence | Meeting structure, Steering Committee, working groups, status reporting, and escalation process. | Delivery Lead / Project Manager |\n| Tools and Access | Required access to Jira, Confluence, Slack or Teams, SFCC Business Manager, repositories, and supporting platforms. | PMO / Technical Lead |\n| Technical Setup | Development environment, code repository, deployment process, sandbox access, and integration points. | Technical Lead |\n| Ways of Working | Delivery ceremonies, documentation standards, issue management, decision tracking, and collaboration expectations. | Project Manager / Workstream Leads |\n\nNew Joiner Checklist\n--------------------\n\n64\n4f41da8a\nincomplete\nConfirm role, workstream, and reporting line.\n\n65\n40be348b\nincomplete\nReview the SFCC Migration project overview and delivery roadmap.\n\n66\n0a41aacf\nincomplete\nRequest access to required project tools and communication channels.\n\n67\n368fd9ce\nincomplete\nJoin relevant project meetings and distribution lists.\n\n68\n48fb810e\nincomplete\nReview governance, status reporting, RAID, and decision management processes.\n\n69\n35b21c9b\nincomplete\nComplete role-specific technical or business onboarding steps.\n\n70\n1026fa5d\nincomplete\nSchedule introductory sessions with the Project Manager, PMO, and relevant workstream lead.\n\nSuggested Child Pages\n---------------------\n\n* Project Overview and Scope\n* Team Directory and Roles\n* Ways of Working\n* Tools and Access Guide\n* Technical Environment Setup\n* Governance and Meeting Cadence\n* Workstream Onboarding Guides\n* FAQs for New Joiners\n\n**Next step:** Use this section as the landing page for all onboarding materials. Add links to detailed child pages as they are created and keep access instructions, ownership, and project contacts up to date.",
