{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "269287425",
    "title": "1.1 Purpose, Objectives, Scope & Success Criteria",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/269287425",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 2,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "This section provides an overview of the SFCC Migration project, including its purpose, scope, objectives, key stakeholders, timeline, and success criteria.\n\n### At a Glance\n\nZimmermann - an Australian luxury fashion house - is replacing its ageing Magento 2 e-commerce platform with a modern, headless, composable architecture built on Salesforce Commerce Cloud (SFCC), with a PWA Kit storefront hosted on Managed Runtime (MRT). We go live across seven global storefronts via a single coordinated launch in January 2027.\n\n### Zimmermann\n\nZimmermann is a premium Australian fashion brand (founded Sydney, 1991) known for ready-to-wear and swim/resort collections, presenting in Paris and operating **~70 boutiques** across Australia, the US, UK, Europe, and the Middle East. E-commerce is a vital extension of the boutique experience. The business runs on frequent seasonal \"drops\" (Spring/Fall/Resort RTW; Summer/Resort Swim), so the platform must handle rapid, multi-region content and catalogue changes with ~1,600 active SKUs at peak.\n\n**Journey So Far**\n\n1. **Discovery** (5 weeks, Apr–May 2026) - Accenture validated the current state, captured ~858 requirements across 18 workstreams, defined the target architecture, and produced the implementation plan.\n2. **Detailed Design** (4 weeks) - requirements refined into user stories, catalogue/integration/customer structures finalised, environments and CI/CD set up.\n3. **Build** - commences **25 June 2026**, runs through to hypercare close **~mid-February 2027**.\n\n### Purpose\n\nThe current Magento 2 platform has reached its limits and is holding the business back:\n\n* **Performance & scalability** constraints, poor Core Web Vitals, unstable caching/indexing that delays catalogue and content updates.\n* **Heavy customisation** creating long-term maintenance overhead.\n* **Fragmented checkout** - a dual Magento + Global-e model adds complexity and logic duplication.\n* **Fragile integrations** - a mix of API, point-to-point and batch patterns, with limited shared test environments.\n* **Innovation blocked** - the rigid architecture can't easily adopt AI or modern capabilities.\n\nThe purpose of this programme is to give Zimmermann a **scalable, high-performance, future-ready commerce platform** that elevates the client experience across every market, simplifies operations, and creates an API-first foundation for ongoing innovation.\n\n### Objectives - What We’re Trying to Achieve\n\n1. A **high-performance, mobile-first** global commerce platform that meets Zimmermann's brand and client-experience standards in every region.\n2. A **scalable, headless, composable, API-first architecture** that integrates cleanly with the wider digital ecosystem.\n3. A modern **SSR-capable PWA Kit frontend** consuming content from Contentful and commerce data from SFCC.\n4. **Global localisation** - regional configuration for translations, pricing, currency, tax, payment, shipping and regulatory compliance.\n5. **Seamless, governed integration** across all systems via the MuleSoft layer.\n6. **Operational efficiency** - simplified workflows, automated testing, CI/CD deployment and clear release governance (removing today's environment contention).\n7. **Data consistency** across channels for unified product, order and client information.\n8. A foundation for **AI-driven personalisation and automation**.\n9. **Measurable business outcomes** — improved conversion, faster page loads, faster content publishing, and lower total cost of ownership.",
      "format": "markdown"
    }
  }
}"}

{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "313589763",
    "title": "Definition of Ready",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/313589763",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 1,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "The Definition of Ready (DoR) sets the minimum criteria a user story must meet before sprint planning. Stories not meeting all criteria are not Ready and return to refinement until they do.\n\nThis standard applies to both squads.\n\n| Criteria | Description | Verified by |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Business requirements clear | The business need and user outcome are clearly understood by the squad. No open questions remain on what the story is meant to achieve. | BA |\n| Acceptance criteria defined | Acceptance criteria are written in Gherkin format — Given / When / Then. Lead QA has reviewed and signed off the feature file before the story is marked Ready. | BA + Lead QA |\n| PO approved | The Product Owner has reviewed and approved the story and its acceptance criteria. Story is aligned to the sprint goal and PI objectives.    PO varies based on the content of the User Story. Refer to <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/x/A4CXDw> | PO |\n| Design available | UX designs, wireframes, or mockups are attached or linked to the story where required. Stories with UI components are not Ready without approved designs. | BA, UX, Developer |\n| Technical approach understood | The squad has a shared understanding of how the story will be built. For complex or unfamiliar work, a spike has been completed and findings documented in Confluence. | Dev Lead / Architect |\n| Dependencies identified | All dependencies are named in the story — internal, cross-squad, or third party. Each dependency has a confirmed owner and expected delivery date or is explicitly flagged as at-risk. | SM, BA |\n| Testable | The story can be tested against the acceptance criteria. Test data, environments, and access required are confirmed available for the sprint. | Lead QA, QA |\n| Estimated | Story points have been assigned during backlog refinement using Planning Poker. Stories with no estimate are not Ready and will not enter planning. | Squad |",
      "format": "markdown"
    }
  }
}"}

