      "value": "Jira Bugs Workflow for SFCC Project\n===================================\n\nThis page explains the expected Jira workflow for bugs in the SFCC project, including what each status means and the actions expected from the team while a bug is in that state.\n\n| Stage in board | Jira Workflow Status | Expected actions during this state |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Backlog | To Do | Bug has been logged in the SFCC project. Confirm the summary, description, priority, affected environment, component, and supporting evidence such as screenshots, logs, order numbers, or steps to reproduce. |\n| Refinement | Triage | Review the bug for validity, severity, business impact, duplicates, and completeness. Assign ownership and determine whether more information is required before analysis can start. |\n| Development | In Progress | Developer implements the fix, updates code or configuration, adds or updates tests where applicable, and keeps Jira comments current with progress, risks, and blockers. |\n| Development | Code Review | Fix is submitted for peer review. Review code quality, SFCC standards, regression risk, performance, security, and deployment notes before merging. |\n| Testing | Ready for QA | Fix is merged and deployed to the agreed test environment. QA validates that the build, environment, test data, and release notes are ready before starting verification. |\n| Testing | In QA | QA verifies the original defect, performs focused regression testing, captures evidence, and raises any retest failures or new linked defects if the issue is not resolved. If the issue is not resolved ticket is moved back to In Progress and assigned back to developer.  QA confirms the bug fix has passed in the test environment. Attach test evidence, update comments. |\n| Done | Done | Fix has been released or otherwise completed according to the agreed process. Confirm validation, close linked work, and ensure all required evidence and comments are available in Jira. |",
      "format": "markdown"
    }
  }
}"}

